/*
 * format — pretty-printing utilities for error locations.
 *
 * This module provides all formatting routines used to display compiler
 * diagnostics with highlighted source excerpts. It handles:
 *
 *   - single-location errors,
 *   - multi-location errors(e.g., matching parentheses),
 *   - EOF locations,
 *   - underline highlighting,
 *   - caret positioning,
 *   - tab-aware spacing,
 *   - line extraction from in-memory file content.
 *
 * All functions write directly into a Formatter stream and return it for
 * chaining. No file I/O is performed; the Word object is assumed to contain
 * the relevant slice of the file content.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::errors::format
 * @File: ymirc/errors/format.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
